# CI and Testing

**Canonical gate details:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) — GitHub Cloud CI is authoritative; local `pnpm quality` is optional pre-check.

## Quick commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `pnpm ci:light` | PR gate mirror (fast) |
| `pnpm ci:check` | lint → typecheck → test:ci → build |
| `pnpm quality` | Full main gate (+ security, audit) |
| `pnpm quality:quiet` | Same as quality; agent-friendly summary on failure |
| `pnpm lint` / `typecheck` / `test` / `test:security` | Individual steps |
| `pnpm file-size:check` | Anti-monolith gate (~5 s, no install) |

## Test expectations

- Bug fixes: regression test when practical.
- New features: tests or documented manual QA in PR.
- Security changes: `pnpm test:security`.
- `packages/database` changes: `pnpm --filter @uwe/database db:generate` before typecheck.

## Rules

- No fake/no-op CI scripts; fix root causes.
- Commit `pnpm-lock.yaml` after dependency changes.
- Prisma schema → migrations in `packages/database/prisma/migrations/`.

